 "asked_at": "2026-10-18T00:45+08:00",
 "answer": "If you mean **Sunday evening, October 18** in Kuching, I can’t say yet that it will be safe: it’s only just after midnight there, and the haze may change before your ride. The latest Kuching station reading I could verify was **77 on Malaysia’s Air Pollutant Index (API), “Moderate,” at 11 p.m. Saturday**. ([semakapi.my](https://semakapi.my/en/kuching))\n\n**Check the Department of Environment’s APIMS reading just before you leave.** If the API is still below 100 and you’re healthy, a shorter, easy-paced ride is a reasonable choice. If it rises **above 100**, ride indoors or postpone: Malaysia’s Ministry of Health advises avoiding outdoor activity at that level. If you have asthma, heart or lung disease, or develop coughing or breathlessness, skip the outdoor ride even at a lower reading. ([eqms.doe.gov.my](https://eqms.doe.gov.my/apims/main?utm_source=openai))",
